WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:04.800
The ocean.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.200
It covers three quarters of our planet.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.500
It gives us the oxygen we breathe.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.000
It regulates our climate.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.000
It feeds us.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:21.500
The ocean gives us clean energy.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.500
It offers new medicines.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.200
For millions, it provides a livelihood.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.400
For millions more, it provides life.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.000
The ocean is owned by no one,

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.500
but shared by everyone.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:49.000
My ocean

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.500
But the ocean is under pressure.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:58.500
Urgent action is needed.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.000
This October global actors will meet in Malta.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:05.800
They know that protecting the seas

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:09.200
means protecting our future.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:12.000
Now, it is the turn of the European Union

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:14.200
to host the 'Our Ocean' conference.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:17.500
Together we will commit to new actions

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:19.700
to protect marine life.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:21.700
To tackle marine litter.

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:26.000
To use our ocean sustainably.

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:30.000
Now more than ever,

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:34.000
my ocean is our ocean

